{"raw": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205233345940_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Marching Band Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nJob Title:\u00a0 Marching Band Visual & Percussion Instructor Employee Class:\u00a0 Seasonal-Athletics Department:\u00a0 Athletics \u2013 Marching Band FLSA Status:\u00a0 Hourly Reports To:\u00a0 Marching Band Director \u00a0 Effective: \u00a0 PRIMARY PURPOSE: The Marching Band Visual & Percussion Instructor is a key member of the marching band instructional team, supporting both visual execution and percussion instruction. This position plays a vital role in the development of the drumline and overall field performance, working closely with the Marching Band Director, student leadership, and band members to ensure an exceptional performance and educational experience. Responsibilities include teaching and refining marching and playing techniques, mentoring student leaders, leading sectionals and rehearsals, and supporting performance logistics. Instruction and Teaching: Teach and refine marching techniques including posture, stride, alignment, and visual precision. Instruct the drumline in playing technique, marching technique, and performance readiness. Provide individualized feedback to students to improve musical and visual performance. Conduct field rehearsals, sectionals, and full ensemble rehearsals for both visual and percussion execution. Attend rehearsals and performances for quality control and fine-tuning. Drill & Visual Implementation: Assist with teaching and cleaning field drill, including accurate placement and movement of performers. Utilize technology (e.g., drone footage, Pyware, rehearsal software) to enhance visual performance. Lead on-field warm-ups and coordinate pre-show routines. Leadership Development: Mentor student leaders, including drum majors and section leaders, to enhance their instructional and leadership capabilities. Facilitate workshops to build leadership, instructional skills, and team culture. Coordination and Logistics: Assist in planning and execution of band camp, rehearsals, and performances. Ensure appropriate use of field equipment including field markers, metronomes, and sound systems. Support organization and transportation of equipment for performances and travel. Student Support & Program Promotion Monitor academic, social, and personal development of band members. Help with student recruitment and evaluation. Assist in building relationships with alumni, donors, and the community to promote the band program. Collaboration and Communication: Work closely with the Director of Bands to align field activities with the program\u2019s artistic and educational goals. Maintain clear and consistent communication with student leadership and staff regarding rehearsal schedules, expectations, and adjustments. EDUCATION: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Music, Music Education, or a related field required. Significant experience in the marching arts may suffice. Master\u2019s degree a plus. EXPERIENCE: Previous experience in teaching marching techniques and drill design/implementation at the high school or collegiate level required. Experience in drumline instruction, visual design, or drill implementation strongly preferred. Familiarity with marching band drill design software (Pyware) and field technology. Experience as a performer or staff member in a collegiate marching band or drum corps. Proven success in mentoring student leaders and fostering a positive band culture. CERTIFICATION:\u00a0 N/A PHYSICAL SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Ability to demonstrate marching and playing techniques, including prolonged standing and movement on the field. Capacity to lift and transport field equipment as needed. WORKING CONDITIONS: Work is performed indoors and outdoors with potential for outdoor exposure to high temperatures, and safety and health hazards related to band instruction. Evening and weekend work is required during marching season. Outdoor rehearsals in varying weather conditions. Travel for performances and recruiting events as necessary. \u00a0 The responsibilities and requirements listed above are not an exhaustive list of all that will be expected of this position; however, it is met to identify the general criteria for this position.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205232565928_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Faculty Position-Asst. Professor of History", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nThe History Department at Ave Maria University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of History position to start in the 2027-2028 academic year. Preference will be given to: Candidates with expertise in a subfield of American history. Candidates who have earned a doctoral degree in History or a closely related field. Candidates with some teaching experience and a promising research agenda. Candidates equipped to contribute to the University\u2019s Catholic identity and mission. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States for full consideration. The following documents must be submitted: - Cover Letter - Curriculum Vitae, including a list of publications - Graduate and Undergraduate University Transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable initially, official transcripts to be furnished upon request) - Teaching Philosophy as it Relates to the Apostolic Constitution Ex Corde Ecclesiae - Research Statement: Research in progress and further interests - Three Letters of Recommendation -Optional supporting materials: Sample syllabi from courses taught, course evaluations Review of applications will begin on November 1 st , 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Rank and salary will be commensurate with the candidate\u2019s credentials. Ave Maria University is a private Catholic university offering over 30 majors, including master\u2019s and doctoral degrees. A Newman Guide School faithful to the Catholic Church\u2019s Magisterium, our university provides one of the strongest classical liberal arts curricula in the country, as well as exceptional opportunities for specialized study in the sciences and humanities. The campus is located in sunny Southwest Florida, in the vibrant and growing town of Ave Maria, Florida. Contact Information Dr. Paul Baxa Chair, Department of History Email: Paul.Baxa@avemaria.edu", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205231192048_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Faculty Position-Finance/Business Admin", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-28\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nFaculty Position-Finance/Business Administration The Business Department at Ave Maria University invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, non-tenured faculty position to start in the 2027-2028 academic year. Preference will be given to: Candidates with teaching, industry, and research experience. Candidates who have earned a doctoral degree in Finance or a closely related field. Candidates equipped to contribute to the University\u2019s Catholic identity and mission. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States for full consideration. The following documents must be submitted: - Cover Letter - Curriculum Vitae, including a list of publications - Graduate and Undergraduate University Transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable initially, official transcripts to be furnished upon request) - Teaching Philosophy as it Relates to the Apostolic Constitution Ex Corde Ecclesiae - Research Statement: Research in progress and further interests - Three Letters of Recommendation -Optional supporting materials: Sample syllabi from courses taught, course evaluations Review of applications will begin on November 1 st , 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Rank and salary will be commensurate with the candidate\u2019s credentials. Ave Maria University is a private Catholic university offering over 30 majors, including master\u2019s and doctoral degrees. A Newman Guide School faithful to the Catholic Church\u2019s Magisterium, our university provides one of the strongest classical liberal arts curricula in the country, as well as exceptional opportunities for specialized study in the sciences and humanities. The campus is located in sunny Southwest Florida, in the vibrant and growing town of Ave Maria, Florida. Contact Information Dr. TJ Iijima Chair, Department of Business Administration Email: Timothy.Iijima@avemaria.edu", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205228932509_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Faculty Position-Mechanical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nThe Mechanical Engineering Program at Ave Maria University invites applications for a full-time, open rank, non-tenured faculty position to start in the 2027-2028 academic year. The position requires both research and teaching of Mechanical Engineering subject matters at the undergraduate level in the following areas: - Machine Design and Material Sciences - Thermal Sciences Preference will be given to candidates with relevant industry and research experience having earned a doctorate degree in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States for full consideration. The following documents must be submitted: - Cover Letter - Curriculum Vitae and List of Publications - Graduate and Undergraduate University Transcripts - Teaching Philosophy as it Relates to the Apostolic Constitution Ex Corde Ecclesiae - Undergraduate Research Statement - Three Letters of Recommendation Review of applications will begin in the fall of 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Rank and salary will be commensurate with the candidate\u2019s credentials. Ave Maria University is a private Catholic university offering over 30 majors, including master\u2019s and doctoral degrees. A Newmann Guide School faithful to the Catholic Church\u2019s magisterium, our university provides one of the strongest classical liberal arts curricula in the country, as well as exceptional opportunities for specialized study in the sciences and humanities. The campus is located in sunny Southwest Florida, in the vibrant and growing town of Ave Maria Florida. Contact Information Alex Tsai, PhD, PE Director of Mechanical Engineering, AMU alex.tsai@avemaria.edu", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205228509861_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Public Services Librarian", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nThe Public Service Librarian manages the activities and operations of the Library. This staff member's work involves circulation, reference, online services, bibliographic instruction, course reserves, and interlibrary loan/document delivery. \u00a0 \u00a0 ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:\u00a0 Supervises all aspects of Public Services. Establishes policies, standards, and procedures for the department in all areas of public service. \u00a0 Provides reference and research assistance to patrons. Provides library instruction when called upon by academic faculty. Serves as public services liaison with faculty, soliciting faculty input and coordinating academic initiatives between library and academics. Establishes and maintains access to electronic resources. \u00a0 Oversees the physical layout of the public area of the library. \u00a0 Runs and analyzes library usage statistics. Serves as Systems Librarian for the library\u2019s Integrated Library System (WorldShare Management System). Maintains the library\u2019s website. Takes the lead in hiring and training staff. EDUCATION: Bachelor\u2019s degree from four-year college. Master\u2019s degree from an ALA-accredited library program or equivalent . EXPERIENCE:\u00a0 At least three years spent professionally in an academic environment, either in the Library or at an academic position. Supervisory experience strongly preferred. CERTIFICATION:\u00a0 Master\u2019s degree from an ALA-Accredited program or equivalent. \u00a0 PHYSICAL SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Position requires sitting for long periods of time and the visual and manual ability to use a computer keyboard. Requires ordinary ambulatory skills sufficient to visit other locations; or the ability to stand, walk and manipulate (lift, carry, move) weights of up to 40 lbs and the ability to push a fully loaded book cart. Packing and unpacking boxes of books may be required.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205226383124_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Professor of Latin", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nAve Maria University seeks applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position teaching elementary and intermediate Latin. Qualified candidates will possess a master\u2019s degree or terminal degree in the field. Candidates with teaching experience in higher education are strongly preferred. TO APPLY :\u202f \u202fApplicants should register here within the Ave Maria University\u2019s online talent management site and upload their cover letter, curriculum vitae, three references, and a statement relating the University\u2019s Catholic mission as expressed in\u202f Ex Corde Ecclesiae \u202fto their philosophy of teaching addressed to: Dr. Bradley Ritter, Chair and Associate Professor of Classics and Early Christian Literature, at Bradley.Ritter@avemaria.edu, Ave Maria University, 5050 Ave Maria Blvd., Ave Maria, FL 34142. \u202f\u202f Review of applications will continue until the position is filled.\u202f Incomplete applications will not be considered. Ave Maria University does not discriminate in employment opportunities, practices, or the terms and conditions of employment based on race, color, sex, national origin, age, disability, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205220096324_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Professor of History", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-23\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nAve Maria University seeks applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position in History. Qualified candidates will possess a master\u2019s degree or terminal degree in history. Candidates with teaching experience in higher education are strongly preferred. TO APPLY :\u202f \u202fApplicants should register here within the Ave Maria University\u2019s online talent management site and upload their cover letter, curriculum vitae, three references, and a statement relating the University\u2019s Catholic mission as expressed in\u202f Ex Corde Ecclesiae \u202fto their philosophy of teaching addressed to: Dr. Paul Baxa, Chair and Professor of History, at Paul.Baxa@avemaria.edu, Ave Maria University, 5050 Ave Maria Blvd., Ave Maria, FL 34142. \u202f\u202f Review of applications will continue until the position is filled.\u202f Incomplete applications will not be considered. Ave Maria University does not discriminate in employment opportunities, practices or the terms and conditions of employment based on race, color, sex, national origin, age, disability, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local law.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205205829936_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Fleet Mechanic", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-05\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nPRIMARY PURPOSE: Ave Maria University is seeking a dependable, hands-on Fleet Mechanic to join our Operations team. This position is responsible for performing preventive maintenance, inspections, and minor repairs on a diverse fleet of landscape equipment, golf carts, utility vehicles, aerial lifts, and other small motorized assets. The Fleet Mechanic will also support parts inventory management, vendor coordination, and light welding or fabrication work as needed. This is an excellent opportunity for an early-career mechanic to grow within a mission-driven university environment.\u00a0 ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: \u00a0 Perform scheduled preventive maintenance on landscape equipment, golf carts, lifts, utility vehicles, and other fleet assets in accordance with manufacturer specifications and university standards. Diagnose and complete minor mechanical, electrical, and hydraulic repairs to maintain fleet readiness and minimize downtime. Conduct routine fleet inspections and document findings; maintain accurate service records within the university\u2019s computerized maintenance management system (Asset Essentials). Develop and maintain a preventive maintenance schedule for all fleet assets, ensuring compliance with safety and regulatory requirements. Manage parts inventory levels, place orders, and coordinate with vendors to ensure timely availability of parts and supplies. Perform light welding, fabrication, and modification work to support equipment repairs and minor operational projects. Maintain a clean, organized, and safe shop environment in accordance with OSHA standards and university policies. Communicate equipment status, repair timelines, and any safety concerns to the Fleet Supervisor in a timely manner. Support other Operations team functions as needed, including occasional assistance with Facilities and Grounds projects. EDUCATION: High school diploma or GED equivalent required. EXPERIENCE: One to two (1\u20132) years of hands-on experience in equipment maintenance, small engine repair, or a related mechanical trade. CERTIFICATION: Valid Florida driver\u2019s license with a clean driving record. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: \u00a0 Minimum Qualifications Basic knowledge of gasoline and small diesel engines, electrical systems, hydraulics, and drivetrain components. Ability to read and interpret equipment manuals, parts diagrams, and service bulletins. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and work in outdoor Florida conditions, including heat and humidity. Preferred Qualifications Experience servicing golf carts (gas and electric), zero-turn mowers, string trimmers, blowers, and similar landscape equipment. Small engine certification or manufacturer-specific training (e.g., Stihl, Toro, Club Car, E-Z-GO). Diesel engine repair experience (light- to medium-duty). Basic MIG/stick welding and fabrication skills. Experience using a CMMS or work order system to log and track maintenance activities. Familiarity with OSHA safety standards for shop and equipment operations. Key Competencies Safety-First Mindset \u2013 Consistently follows safe work practices and identifies hazards proactively. Reliability \u2013 Demonstrates strong attendance, punctuality, and follow-through on assigned tasks. Problem-Solving \u2013 Approaches mechanical issues methodically and resourcefully. Communication \u2013 Provides clear, timely updates on work status and escalates issues appropriately. Teamwork \u2013 Works cooperatively with Grounds, Facilities, and other Operations staff. Continuous Improvement \u2013 Willing to learn new skills, pursue certifications, and adopt better maintenance practices. PHYSICAL SKILLS AND ABILITIES: This position requires regular standing, walking, bending, kneeling, and lifting up to 50 pounds. Work is performed both indoors (shop environment) and outdoors in varying weather conditions. \u00a0 WORKING CONDITIONS: The role involves regular exposure to noise, fumes, oils, chemicals, and moving mechanical parts. Appropriate personal protective equipment (PPE) will be provided and is required at all times. Ave Maria University is a Catholic institution of higher education. Ave Maria University makes employment decisions in a manner that is consistent with federal, state and local law. All information included in any application must be truthful and accurate.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205198181107_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Director of Marching Band", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-12\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nPRIMARY PURPOSE: The Director of Marching Band is responsible for the creation, implementation, leadership, and administration of the university\u2019s marching band program and related instrumental ensembles. This part-time position provides artistic, educational, operational, and strategic oversight while supporting the mission of Ave Maria University and enhancing campus spirit, student engagement, and institutional visibility. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: \u00a0 Program Development Establish and implement the vision, structure, and operational framework for the university marching band program Develop strategic plans for program growth, recruitment, retention, and sustainability Create traditions, performance standards, and organizational culture for the program Student Recruitment and Retention Recruit qualified student musicians through outreach to high schools, music educators, and prospective students Collaborate with admissions, athletics, and campus leadership on recruitment initiatives Develop retention strategies and student leadership opportunities Instruction and Performance Conduct and direct marching band rehearsals and performances Direct additional ensembles including concert band, jazz band, pep band, and other instrumental groups as assigned Select music, coordinate drill design, and oversee show development Evaluate student performance and provide mentoring and instruction Administrative Management Prepare and manage annual operating budgets Oversee purchasing, inventory, equipment, uniforms, instruments, and facilities Coordinate travel, scheduling, contracts, and event logistics Ensure compliance with university policies and safety procedures Personnel Management Recruit, supervise, and evaluate assistant directors and student leaders as assigned Institutional Engagement Represent the university at performances, outreach events, and community functions Collaborate with university departments to support institutional events and student engagement initiatives EDUCATION: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Music, Music Education, Conducting, or related field. Master\u2019s degree preferred.\u00a0 EXPERIENCE: Minimum of 3\u20135 years of progressively responsible experience directing marching bands, concert bands, jazz ensembles, or related instrumental music programs, preferably at the high school or collegiate level. Experience with performance planning, rehearsal design, and event coordination.\u00a0 CERTIFICATION:\u00a0 N/A KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES:\u00a0 Demonstrated success in marching band instruction and leadership. Strong organizational, communication, and administrative skills. Ability to work evenings and weekends, as needed. Experience in drill design, arranging, budgeting, and personnel supervision. Must support the University\u2019s Catholic mission.\u00a0 PHYSICAL SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Requires ordinary ambulatory skills sufficient to visit other locations. Ability to stand for extended periods. Ability to conduct rehearsals and performances outdoors in varied weather conditions. Ability to lift and transport equipment up to 30 pounds. WORKING CONDITIONS: Work is performed both indoors and outdoors with exposure to outdoor elements typical to our location in SW Florida; heat, humidity, rain, etc. \u00a0 Ave Maria University is a Catholic institution of higher education. Ave Maria University makes employment decisions in a manner that is consistent with federal, state and local law. All information included in any application must be truthful and accurate. \u00a0 The responsibilities and requirements listed above are not an exhaustive list of all that will be expected of this position; however, it is met to identify the general criteria for this position.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201305005522_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing", "description": "Posted: 2025-08-27\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nAve Maria University seeks applicants for a full-time position in Nursing. \u00a0Applicants with a doctoral degree in Nursing are preferred. \u00a0 A master\u2019s degree in nursing is acceptable. \u00a0Applicants with a minimum of three years of clinical nursing experience, experience as a preceptor, or educator are preferred. Experience in simulation and clinical skills instruction and debriefing is desired. Certification in Basic Cardiac Life Support (BCLS) is required; certified instructors in Basic Cardiac Life Support (BCLS) are preferred. Knowledge of clinical practice, quality improvement, patient safety initiatives. and evidence-based care of multicultural populations are strongly preferred. Ideal candidates will possess expertise in Maternal, Pediatric, and/or Medical/Surgical Care, and will have the ability to teach a broad range of courses in nursing. \u00a0 Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, three references willing to supply letters upon request, and a short statement relating the University\u2019s Catholic mission to their philosophy of the curriculum as expressed in Ex Corde Ecclesiae . Questions should be directed to Dr. DiAnn Ecret, DiAnn.Ecret@avemaria.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The position is subject to final administrative approval. Those who received any graduate degrees from an institution outside the United States must provide a foreign course-by-course credential evaluation by an independent evaluation service that is a member of the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). \u00a0Find a full list of NACES members at http://www.naces.org/members.htm .", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200595850645_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Internal Only - Adjunct Positions", "description": "Posted: 2022-09-12\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nPlease note this posting is used for newly hired Adjuncts at Ave Maria University. \u00a0 If not already hired and you are interested in searching current job positions available at the University, please visit our website at www.avemaria.edu/employment .", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200351494632_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "On Campus Ave Maria University Student Worker", "description": "Posted: 2022-01-06\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nThis requisition is part of the hiring process for Ave Maria University students who have already been offered a position. It is used to collect the information needed by the Human Resources Department to complete your employment and onboarding. When you click the Apply button, uploading a cover letter is optional . If you do not wish to upload one, simply click Next at the bottom of the screen to continue.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205244256323_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Part-Time Security Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nPRIMARY PURPOSE:\u00a0 Ave Maria University is seeking a dependable and service-oriented individual to join our Department of Safety and Security team as a Part-Time Day Shift Security Officer. This is an unarmed position. The officer is responsible for maintaining a safe, secure, and welcoming campus environment, serving as a visible, professional presence on campus, responding to incidents and emergencies, and supporting the overall mission of the University by upholding its Catholic identity and values. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: \u25cf Conduct regular foot and vehicle patrols of the campus, including buildings, parking lots, residence halls, and grounds, to deter unauthorized activity and ensure the safety of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. \u25cf Monitor and control access to campus facilities, verifying the identity and authorization of individuals seeking entry. \u25cf Respond promptly to alarms, emergency calls, reports of suspicious activity, and requests for assistance; coordinate with local law enforcement and emergency services as needed. \u25cf Prepare accurate and timely written incident reports documenting observations, actions taken, and any policy violations or safety concerns observed during the shift. \u25cf Assist in maintaining compliance with applicable safety regulations. \u25cf Provide courteous assistance and information to students and campus community members, reflecting the University\u2019s commitment to hospitality and service. \u25cf Secure and lock campus buildings and facilities at designated times in accordance with established procedures. \u25cf Perform other duties as assigned by the Safety and Security Coordinator or university leadership. EDUCATION: \u25cf High school diploma or GED equivalent required. \u25cf Valid Florida driver\u2019s license without any serious traffic offenses within the last 3 years. \u25cf Ability to pass a background check. \u25cf Ability to work overnight shifts, including weekends and holidays. \u25cf Strong written and verbal communication skills; ability to prepare clear and accurate incident reports. \u25cf Physical ability to patrol campus on foot, bicycle and by vehicle, including climbing stairs and remaining alert during overnight hours. \u25cf Commitment to upholding the Catholic mission and values of Ave Maria University. EXPERIENCE: \u00a0 Preferred: Prior experience in campus security, law enforcement, military, or related field. Familiarity with campus safety systems, access control technology, or security software. CERTIFICATION: CPR/First Aid certification or willingness to obtain upon hire. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Exceptional time management and organization skills Ability to work independently, collaboratively, and under supervision. Willingness to serve, and build relationships with the troupe Must possess strong initiative, leadership skills, organizational and project management skills, with the ability to multitask to manage a variety of projects and priorities, coordinating the actions of others, follow through on projects to timely completion and demonstrate excellent judgment with attention to detail. Must support the University\u2019s Catholic mission. PHYSICAL SKILLS AND ABILITIES: The officer must be able to stand, walk, and remain active for extended periods. The position requires alertness and professionalism. The position may require occasional lifting of up to 30 pounds and operation of a campus vehicle. WORKING CONDITIONS: This position requires working outdoors in varying Florida weather conditions, including heat and humidity. The officer must be able to stand, walk, and remain active for extended periods. The position requires alertness and professionalism. The position may require occasional lifting of up to 30 pounds and operation of a campus vehicle. \u00a0 Ave Maria University is a Catholic institution of higher education. Ave Maria University makes employment decisions in a manner that is consistent with federal, state and local law. All information included in any application must be truthful and accurate. \u00a0 The responsibilities and requirements listed above are not an exhaustive list of all that will be expected of this position; however, it is met to identify the general criteria for this position.", "department": ""}}, "rows": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205233345940_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 217, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205233345940_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Marching Band Assistant", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-09-04", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205232565928_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 217, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205232565928_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Faculty Position-Asst. Professor of History", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "History", "deadline_of_application": "November 1, 2026", "posted_date": "2026-09-02", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforc